From: port (2026-10-25)
Subject: [PATCH] 0077 on KWin 6.8.1: AnimationClock::tick has a zero-delta return inside the last-timestamp
 branch there (71cbc668); the first-tick step follows that branch

From: Local <local@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] EXP: effects: an animation's first frame one refresh in, at run time (host)

Stock AnimationClock::tick() returns 0 on its first call, so every effect animation renders its first frame at
progress 0 - the state before the animation. On the host (Arc Pro B50, 2026-10-23) the launcher's slide-in showed
its first change only at the third composited frame after the popup's first buffer. With KWIN_ANIMATION_START_STEP=1
(as in the guests, patch 0037) or "1" in $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kwin-animation-start-step, the first tick returns one
refresh interval. The host's 0037 without the steady animation clock it builds on.
---
diff --git a/src/effect/timeline.cpp b/src/effect/timeline.cpp
index d650249b82..312dd9de29 100644
--- a/src/effect/timeline.cpp
+++ b/src/effect/timeline.cpp
@@ -9,9 +9,34 @@
 
 using namespace std::chrono_literals;
 
+#include <QFile>
+#include <QStandardPaths>
+
 namespace KWin
 {
 
+// An animation's first frame one refresh in: at zero it shows the state before the animation - a sliding popup
+// still hidden, a window still where it was - so the screen repeats an image and every animation starts a refresh
+// late (the launcher's slide-in: two composited frames without a change, 2026-10-23). On with
+// KWIN_ANIMATION_START_STEP=1 (the guests' variable) or "1" in $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kwin-animation-start-step, read at
+// an animation's first tick at most once a second (the host's environment is fixed at login).
+static bool startOneRefreshIn()
+{
+    static const bool env = qEnvironmentVariableIntValue("KWIN_ANIMATION_START_STEP") == 1;
+    if (env) {
+        return true;
+    }
+    static std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point checked;
+    static bool file = false;
+    const auto now = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+    if (checked == std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point() || now - checked > std::chrono::seconds(1)) {
+        checked = now;
+        QFile f(QStandardPaths::writableLocation(QStandardPaths::RuntimeLocation) + QStringLiteral("/kwin-animation-start-step"));
+        file = f.open(QIODevice::ReadOnly) && f.read(1) == "1";
+    }
+    return file;
+}
+
 AnimationClock::AnimationClock()
 {
 }
@@ -33,6 +58,8 @@ std::chrono::milliseconds AnimationClock::tick(std::chrono::nanoseconds timestam
             // don't progress with a difference of 0ms, or it'll round away everything
             return 0ms;
         }
+    } else if (refreshRate && startOneRefreshIn()) {
+        delta = std::chrono::milliseconds(1000000) / refreshRate;
     }
 
     // Prevent the delta time from getting too big to minimize stuttering. If we have missed a frame,
